HST Office: dialogs keep a minimum gap between stacked and neighbouring controls (dialog layout rulebook).

Spacing properties only (row-spacing, column-spacing, spacing of grids and boxes in dialog and tab-page .ui
files); no widget, id, label, string, order or accessibility change. Values from hst::design::layout:
- two controls with a border (entry, spin button, combo box, list, button) stacked in a grid column or a
  vertical box: RowGap 6 px apart (was 0-5; e.g. the 3 px spin-button stacks of Page Style's margins and
  Paragraph's indents and spacing);
- two such controls side by side: 6 px (was 0-3);
- other stacked controls (labels, check and radio buttons, a check button over an entry): MinGap 4 px at least
  (was 0-3; 6 kept where it was 6). Where margins already add to a pair, only the missing part is set.
The intentional exceptions (a show-password toggle joined to its entry, alternatives shown one at a time...)
are listed with their reasons in tests/unit/data/ui-layout-exceptions.json and left as they are. Checked by
tests/unit/test_ui_layout_rulebook.py (static) and tests/runtime/hst_dialog_layout_check.py (on screen).

